# KNOWN GAP (filed 2026-08-06 by Round XXXII Track D+E output-review B4):
# Bare `v.push(x)` on a `shared` variable OUTSIDE a `with v:` block is a
# SILENT NO-OP -- the push mutates the facade snapshot, not the guarded
# storage, and the next bare read reads back an empty snapshot. Neither
# backend enforces the ratified `docs/language-reference.md:1366` bare-read/
# write reject.
#
#   gg check              : exit 0, no diagnostic
#   gg build (C)          : exit 0
#   gg build --backend=llvm: exit 0
#   run                   : prints `0`
#
# INTENDED: `1` (the push writes through the guarded storage).
#
# This is the WRITE face of the same class as the bare-READ owner-
# reconciliation follow-up (docs/language-reference.md:1366 says the reject
# covers BOTH reads and writes; the WRITE face is arguably worse -- it
# silently drops the mutation, where the read face at least returns a
# defined snapshot value).
#
# Related: `docs/language-reference.md:1366` (the ratified bare-read/write
# reject that neither backend enforces).
#
# Discovered while writing Track D+E's fixture net (Round XXXII, 2026-08-06):
# the brief specified this exact shape for the P4 ArcMutex-Vector-ctor
# class-fix pin, but the runtime output was `0` instead of `1`. The class-
# fix at the CTOR init lowering is exercised identically whether the push
# is wrapped in `with v:` or not (the tmp-mat is at the init site, not the
# push site), so P4 was pinned via `with v:` (see
# `tests/fixtures/shared_vector_ctor_init.gg`) and this bare-write shape
# was filed as a separate defect.
#
# Graduate out of known_gaps/ (un-ignore + move) the round this is fixed.

void main():
    shared Vector[int] v = Vector[int]()
    v.push(1)
    print(v.len())
